  "ordering_asymmetry": {
    "affects": [
      "strict_hit_at_1",
      "relaxed_hit_at_1"
    ],
    "explanation": "sage_single_backend takes all three attempts on one backend, so its early candidates carry that provider's own ranking. sage_governed_multiroute fills its first slots from whichever route answered first, and its route-1 backend (OpenAIRE) frequently returns nothing. A hit@1 gap can therefore reflect candidate ordering rather than backend diversity, so the gate rests on strict_hit_at_10, which is insensitive to order within the cutoff.",
